Expected elements: present

Every MUST SHOW item renders and no MUST NOT SHOW item appears. The dark theme is designed, not inverted: a four-level neutral ladder (#000000 gutters / #1b1b1b pane / #202020 chip / #282828 header), a real editor palette (keyword #93c5fd, type #67e8f9, fn #fbbf24, literal #c4b5fd, comment #22c55e), and a chromatic #334155 current-line band echoed in the selected call-trace row. Colour *roles* are where it fails.

Of the five changes: the flush-left provenance note landed (1157–1428, 248–450; #a2a2a2 on #1b1b1b = 6.75:1); `← demo` landed; the ⊙/⊘ marks landed on one branch pair only; `COST · TRANSACTIONFEE` sits below the y=900 clip and is unverifiable here — the visible `COST · MANA` row is decimal; the decoded-input note is not in this view.

Glyph verdict, measured: ⊘ (75–82, 309–317) #919191 on #1b1b1b = 5.47:1; ⊙ (75–82, 379–387) #06b6d4 on #334155 = 4.26:1 — up from the filed 2.40, so contrast is fixed. Form is not. Both are 8×9px rings with a 1px stroke differing only by a 2×3px interior dot versus a ~7px diagonal; greyscaled onto a common ground they are indistinguishable at 1:1 and separate only above ~2× magnification. They are told apart by hue and by which surface they land on.

One hue still means many things: cyan does seven jobs, including being both the source type token and the current-line marker inside the same pane.

Highest-priority fixes: split the cyan marker role from the cyan syntax role; lift iteration tabs 4–8 off 2.0:1.

Rating: 6/10

